LAYERING (unchanged rules)
- data_object.h + new data_actions.h are the dependency-free contract.
- app_data.c is the only "map": holds every ops table + adapters, delegates to
  context modules. Context modules stay DataObject/DataOps-ignorant.
- app_intrf.c exposes nav_cx_* pass-throughs keyed by ContextId, resolves
  ContextId -> CX -> &cx->data, calls through ops. Knows no specific action.
- ui_layer / cli.c call the nav_cx_* functions.

FIVE DECISIONS (settled)
1. data_actions.h is its own header, included by data_object.h (mirrors
   data_events.h). DataOps references its types.
2. Enumeration calls (list_count/list_at) take the DataListId itself (the
   value the caller already got back in DataArgSpec.list - forwarded
   unchanged, not re-derived from a (type, arg_index) pair) AND a const
   DataActionReq *partial (the half-filled request the UI is already
   assembling) so "list content depends on an earlier arg's value" just
   works. No arg_index / DataActionType param needed on these two calls:
   DataListId alone identifies which list, and partial->type already carries
   the action when anything needs it. Supersedes the standalone arg_index
   point.
3. DataAction.enabled is wired now; return true initially, add module
   predicates (smp_can_remove, ...) lazily. CONNECT.enabled = false when no
   source or no target ports exist.
4. Drop DATA_CAP_RENAME. DATA_CAP_ACTIONS gates the whole action group;
   per-action `enabled` expresses availability.
5. Strings in DataActionReq (and the targets[] array) are borrowed for the
   duration of the action_do call only; the module copies what it keeps.
   Document in the header like name().

IDENTITY / KEYS
- One composition rule everywhere: MAKE_ID(namespace, local), 8-bit ns in top
  byte (CTXID_NS_SHIFT), like ContextId.
- DataListId = MAKE_LIST_ID(list_ns, LID_* constant). List kinds are STATIC ->
  compile-time constants (LID_*), NOT counter-allocated. No next_*_uid for
  lists. A genuinely per-instance list composes an owner id into the local part
  (e.g. MAKE_LIST_ID(DATA_LIST_NS_PORTS, osc_uid)); the starter actions don't.
- DataChoice.value is ALSO namespaced: MAKE_ID(list_ns, item_key). item_key is
  the module's natural STABLE key (hash of LV2/CLAP URI; hash of JACK port name;
  plain index for an immutable list). Not a positional index. Reuse an existing
  per-slot uid only when there is no natural key.
- Two-level staleness in action_do:
    * wrong list  -> CTXID_NS(value) != arg's list namespace -> ERR_INVALID
    * stale item  -> key no longer resolves in the live list -> ERR_STALE
                     (UI re-pulls the list)
  Lists that share a namespace (contextual port lists): action_do additionally
  re-derives the full DataListId from (target ctx + arg) and confirms membership.

data_actions.h  (contract)
    typedef uint64_t DataListId;               // opaque, namespaced
    #define DATA_LIST_NONE ((DataListId)0)

    typedef enum {
        DATA_ACTION_REMOVE,
        DATA_ACTION_ADD_CHOICE,
        DATA_ACTION_ADD_FILE_PATH,
        DATA_ACTION_CONNECT,                    // generic bipartite toggle-connect
        // rename / value-change slot in later
    } DataActionType;

    typedef enum {
        DATA_ARG_STRING, DATA_ARG_PATH,
        DATA_ARG_CHOICE, DATA_ARG_MULTI_CHOICE,
        // DATA_ARG_INT, DATA_ARG_DOUBLE later
    } DataArgKind;

    typedef enum { DATA_ACTION_STYLE_NORMAL, DATA_ACTION_STYLE_DANGEROUS } DataActionStyle;

    typedef enum {
        DATA_ACTION_OK = 0,
        DATA_ACTION_ERR_INVALID,      // bad ctx / action / args / wrong list
        DATA_ACTION_ERR_NOT_ALLOWED,  // action present but not enabled
        DATA_ACTION_ERR_STALE,        // key was valid, item now gone
        DATA_ACTION_ERR_DATA,         // module rejected (file won't load, link failed)
    } DataActionResult;

    typedef struct {                  // one entry in a context's action menu
        DataActionType type;
        const char *label;            // borrowed, static in data layer
        const char *tooltip;
        bool enabled;
        DataActionStyle style;
    } DataAction;

    typedef struct {                  // one input an action needs
        const char *name;             // "path", "source", "targets"
        const char *label;
        DataArgKind kind;
        bool required;
        DataListId list;              // set for CHOICE / MULTI_CHOICE, else DATA_LIST_NONE
    } DataArgSpec;

    typedef struct {                  // one option for a (MULTI_)CHOICE arg
        uint64_t value;               // MAKE_ID(list_ns, stable item_key)
        const char *label;            // borrowed, valid while the module's list lives
        uint32_t flags;               // bit 0: linked to partial->connect.source
                                      // (0 for catalogue lists)
    } DataChoice;

    typedef struct {                  // filled-in request to execute
        DataActionType type;
        union {
            struct { uint64_t choice_value; }                              add_choice;
            struct { const char *path; }                                   add_file_path;
            struct { uint64_t source;                                      // MAKE_ID(domain_ns, key)
                     const uint64_t *targets; size_t target_count; }       connect;
            // remove: no payload
        };
    } DataActionReq;

