  nav_cx_action_do, after the data layer returns:
    1. app_intrf_sync(app_intrf) -- the Phase D synchronous-reconcile
       invariant. Shared with nav_update: data_update() first (action_do only
       flips a module's dirty flag, e.g. smp_add's samples_dirty -
       app_data_update is what turns a dirty flag into a DataEvent, so it has
       to run here rather than waiting for the next per-frame nav_update),
       then app_intrf_process_data_events (drains the DataEvent ring, resync,
       emits CxEvents).
    2. if *out_new was set, only hand it back once ht_get() on it succeeds
       (the resync above is what materialises it) - defensive, else it stays
       CONTEXT_ID_NULL rather than naming a dangling id.
    3. return the DataActionResult unchanged (one type end to end).
  All interface buffers are caller stack. Only heap that moves is inside the
  module when the action genuinely creates state (loading a plugin).
