PORT CONNECTIVITY  (folded into DATA_ACTION_CONNECT, generic from the start)
- Ports/connections are NOT contexts and NOT in the CX tree. They are live
  lists, like the plugin catalogue -- externally driven, churny (MIDI hotplug,
  sources appearing/leaving). Tree nodes here caused real problems before.
- Generic bipartite connect: pick one `source` from list A, pick many `targets`
  from list B that depends on `source`, apply a toggle.
- Domain discriminator = CTXID_NS(req.connect.source). First (only) domain =
  JACK ports, DATA_LIST_NS_PORTS. Future domains (modulation, buses, MIDI
  routing) = new DATA_LIST_NS_* + a case in the hosting ops table; ZERO
  contract change. No per-link scalar, no relationship-type bag -- a domain
  that needs those earns its own action.
- Hosted on the Trk context (already owns trk_jack). No SID_ROUTING singleton.
  CONNECT may appear in other ops tables later, like REMOVE.
- Args: arg0 `source` CHOICE list LID_PORTS_OUT (all output ports, live via
  app_jack_port_names). arg1 `targets` MULTI_CHOICE, list depends on arg0:
  empty until a source is chosen, then type-filtered (audio<->audio,
  midi<->midi via jack_port_type) and each row's flags bit 0 = "already linked
  to source".
- item_key = hash(JACK port name) (globally unique, stable across hotplug).
  value = MAKE_ID(DATA_LIST_NS_PORTS, hash(name)). Data layer keeps a
  name<->hash map (or re-scans + hashes to match; small N).
- action_do(CONNECT): per target -> linked already ? app_jack_disconnect_ports
  : app_jack_connect_ports. Toggle = "option a": the UI selects only the
  targets it wants to CHANGE (matches "connecting an existing connection
  disconnects it"). Return OK if all took, ERR_DATA if any failed; UI re-pulls
  the target list either way. (Option b, "selected = desired set, action_do
  diffs", can be added behind a payload flag later.)
- "Keep the connect window open" = UI loops nav_cx_action_do(CONNECT) +
  re-pull; nothing below the UI is stateful about the session.
- Optional refresh nudge: a JACK port-registration / graph-order callback sets
  ports_dirty -> app_data_update emits DATA_EVENT_CHANGED{ Trk id } ->
  CX_CHANGED{ Trk id } -> connectivity UI_STATE re-pulls. CX_CHANGED, not
  ADDED/REMOVED: no resync, no structural churn. Not needed for v1 if the CLI
  re-pulls each frame while the window is open.

