EXTENSIBILITY BOUNDARY
  The UI only ever learns argument KINDS (STRING/PATH/CHOICE/MULTI_CHOICE, later
  INT/DOUBLE), never action types. New action reusing existing kinds -> one
  enum value + one case in the relevant ops table, ZERO UI change. A new arg
  KIND is the only thing that touches the UI. A genuinely new interaction shape
  (neither "enter a scalar" nor "pick from an enumerable list") is the only
  thing that would justify a new DataOps pointer -- explicit > clever.

